<BaseLayout title="About" description="Hyphos Inc. is Daniel Newton's software company in Okotoks and Calgary. We build software for clients and Hyphos, a platform that keeps knowledge connected to the work.">
<section class="product-editorial-hero page-shell"><p class="section-label">About Hyphos Inc.</p><h1>Good Systems<br />Give People Room</h1><p>Room to think. To care for customers. To do the part of the work that depends on experience and judgment.</p></section>
<section class="product-editorial-body page-shell"><aside class="product-editorial-aside"><p class="section-label">The Person Behind The Work</p><p><strong>Daniel Newton</strong><br />Founder, Hyphos Inc.<br />Okotoks &amp; Calgary, Alberta</p><a href="/contact" class="text-link">Start A Conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside><div class="product-editorial-prose">
  <h2>Start With What People Actually Do</h2>
  <p>The work rarely fits neatly into the software. Someone keeps a spreadsheet on the side. Someone remembers the exception. Someone knows who to call.</p>
  <p>Hyphos starts there. We look at how the business runs, connect the information it depends on, and build software around the work.</p>
  <h2>Stay Close Enough To Build The Right Thing</h2>
  <p>You work directly with Daniel. We talk with the people using the systems, make the problem concrete, and show working software early.</p>
  <p>Some problems need an integration. Some need custom software. Some need a clearer process. The useful answer starts with knowing which one you're facing.</p>
  <h2>The Reason Matters As Much As The Record</h2>
  <p>A plan tells you what the team intends to do. It rarely tells you everything that led there: the exception, the conversation, the lesson from the last job.</p>
  <p>That is the idea behind Hyphos, our platform. The documents, decisions and experience belong in the context of the work they inform, so the next person has something to build on.</p>
  <h2>Two Ways To Work With Us</h2>
  <p><a href="/services">Client work</a> connects operations and builds the tools a business is missing. <a href="/#how-it-works">Hyphos</a> focuses on the knowledge behind the work: decisions, experience and context a team can use again.</p>
  <p>They share one premise. The systems should carry more of the coordination, so people can give their attention to the work that needs them.</p>
  <a href="/work" class="text-link">See The Work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</div></section>
